{
  "dom_id": "step-q114463",
  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "A course grade is calculated by adding the results of a written test, oral test, and colloquium, contributing $50%$, $30%,$ and $20%,$ respectively to the final grade. \n\nThe written test results are normally distributed with a mean of $64$ and a standard deviation of $8.$ The oral test results are normally distributed with a mean of $50$ and a standard deviation of $10$, while the results of the colloquium are normally distributed with a mean of $60$ and a standard deviation of $10.$ Find the probability that a randomly selected student achieves a grade greater than $70.$ You may assume that the scores on each test are independent.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.9\\,$ | $\\,0.9713\\,$ | $\\,0.9719\\,$ | $\\,0.9726\\,$ | $\\,0.9732\\,$ | $\\,0.9738\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.9772\\,$ | $\\,0.9778\\,$ | $\\,0.9783\\,$ | $\\,0.9788\\,$ | $\\,0.9793\\,$ |\n| $\\,2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.9821\\,$ | $\\,0.9826\\,$ | $\\,0.9830\\,$ | $\\,0.9834\\,$ | $\\,0.9838\\,$ |",
